    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">The Euler brick is a special kind of brick where not only are the <var>lenght</var>, <var>width</var> and <var>height</var> of the brick all integers, but so are the diagonals on all <strong>faces</strong>.<br><br>Given the <var>lenght</var>, <var>width</var> and <var>height</var> of a brick, determine if it is an Euler brick. If the given values do not form a brick at all print <const>Not a brick</const>.<br><br>Example: A brick of lengths 44, 117 and 240 has <strong>face</strong> diagonals of 125, 244 and 267, making it an Euler brick.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> three integers corresponding to the <var>lenght</var>, <var>width</var> and <var>height</var> of a brick.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> <const>Euler brick</const> if the brick in question is an Euler brick, <const>Regular Brick</const> if not, <const>Not a brick</const> if the given inputs do not make a brick.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0 &lt;=  <var>lenght</var>,<var>width</var>,<var>height</var> &lt;= 100000</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">44\n117\n240</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">Euler brick</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
